  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Slight Risk of severe thunderstorms Tuesday with a strong\nfrontal passage.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nShortwave ridging aloft should limit thunderstorm coverage this\nafternoon. 18Z NUCAPS data showed relatively steep mid-level\nlapse rates which may result in an isold severe thunderstorm,\nhowever, relatively low 850 mb dewpoints suggest coverage will\nremain very sparse this afternoon into this evening. A quiet\nperiod is anticipated this evening, before the first round of\nshowers and thunderstorms associated with an approaching cold\nfront arrives after 09Z Tue. \n\nA sharpening trough associated with a deepening upper low and\nsfc low over western NY and LK Ontario is expected to promote\nstrong height falls and provide large scale forcing for upward\nvertical motion. Multiple rounds of widespread showers and\nthunderstorms are anticipated through the day into the evening.\nStrengthening mid-level winds will result in an increasingly \nsheared environment to support severe thunderstorms in a \nmoderately unstable environment. While some intense rainfall\nrates are expected, the progressive nature of thunderstorms\nshould limit the threat of flash flooding. Convection should \nstart exiting the area after 00Z Wed as the cold front crosses\nthe area. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A few chances for rain through the weekend, but no hazardous \nweather expected between Wednesday and Sunday at this time. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\n\nThe upper-low over the northeast CONUS will linger through Friday \nbefore finally pulling off to the northeast. As a result, there will \nbe non-zero rain chances each day, primairly areas further north and \neast. Friday could be dry for all, but still a bit of uncertainty \nregarding exactly when the upper low departs. \n\nA broad upper-level trough will begin to form over the Ohio River \nValley over the weekend. As this trough tracks east, cloud cover & \nprecipitation chances will begin to increase, particularly between \nSaturday evening and Sunday as the low tracks offshore and towards \nthe northeast. Severe probabilities look low at this time, with a \npretty weak wind field aloft. Nonetheless, weekend showers are \npossible with this system should the synoptic setup continue to \ntrend toward development over the Midwest.",
